(a) No license or special endorsement issued hereunder shall be suspended or revoked except for due cause as hereinafter defined and after a hearing before city council with at least a three-day written notice to the licensee of the time, place and purpose of the hearing, and a statement of said alleged due cause. Said licensee shall be entitled to appear before council at the hearing both personally and by attorney, shall be entitled to cross-examine witnesses against him/her/it, and shall be entitled to present witnesses in his/her/its own behalf. Due cause for the suspension or revocation of a license shall consist of any of the following:
(1) Violation of any state or federal law, except traffic violations;
(2) Violation of any city or local ordinance other than traffic violations;
(3) Violation of any provision of this chapter;
(4) Any material, false statement, or material omission relating to any license issued hereunder, including, but not limited to, any material, false statement or material omission on any application.
(b) At all hearings for suspension or revocation of any license issued under this Code, council shall consider the following criteria:
(1) The alleged violation(s);
(2) The past history of the licensee;
(3) The materiality of any false statement or omission that may be involved;
(4) The harm or potential harm of the alleged violation;
(5) The number and nature of calls to the police department relating to the licensee;
(6) The harm or potential harm to the public;
(7) The harm or potential harm to the licensee;
(8) The number of past violations or warnings;
(9) The number of past incidents occurring on the premises.
(c) Following said hearing, and after consideration of the above criteria, council may take any of the following actions:
(1) Suspend the license or special endorsement for any period of time, up to the remainder of the license or special endorsement;
(2) Revoke the license or special endorsement;
(3) Issue a warning;
(4) Table the matter.
(d) Any special endorsement shall be automatically suspended without the need for a hearing upon the licensee's failure to timely file any required affidavit.
(Ord. No. 35, 5-21-74; Ord. of 12-1-08, § XIV)

