It shall be unlawful for any sales to be made outside of the building, premises or place of business licensed for such sale.
(a) If, and only if, approved by council and so endorsed on the license, the licensee of a consumption on premises license may serve alcoholic beverages outside the premises in any area that is directly adjacent and contiguous to the licensed premises and which meets all of the following requirements:
(1) Full approval by council;
(2) Has the same address as the licensed premises;
(3) Is owned or leased and is exclusively controlled by the licensee;
(4) Is not public domain nor only nominally under the exclusive control of the licensee;
(5) The alcoholic beverages must be served from the same bar or serving location that services the main premises;
(6) Any consumption on premises licensee applying for such special endorsement shall at least annually, affirm his/her/its meeting these conditions by the filing of an affidavit with the city licensing department. Such affidavit may be filed at any time the above conditions are met by the establishment, but must be filed at least annually, with its license application, and city council may, in its discretion, require monthly filing from any licensee applying for or holding such special endorsement;
(7) No alcoholic beverages shall be sold, served or dispensed at any time in any parking lot, upon any sidewalk, or in any other public area adjacent to the licensed premises, and there shall be no "curb sales".
(Ord. No. 35, 5-21-74; Ord. of 12-1-08, § XIX)

